WEBVTT

00:00:00.291 --> 00:00:03.816
Oxford Bookworms, Stage 1.

00:00:03.876 --> 00:00:10.806
Christmas in Prague, by Joyce Hanham, read by Jill Schilling.

00:00:10.866 --> 00:00:27.568
Published and Copyright, Oxford University Press 2005.

00:00:27.628 --> 00:00:53.466
Chapter 1 Christmas 1957 It is night and the fields near the village are white with snow.

00:00:53.526 --> 00:01:00.086
The village is quiet but not everybody is sleeping.

00:01:00.146 --> 00:01:13.902
Eyes are watching the roads and the fields near the village because this is Czechoslovakia and the year is 1957.

00:01:13.962 --> 00:01:30.199
Across the fields, only half a kilometre away is the Austrian border, but the people of Czechoslovakia are not free to go to Austria.

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:44.702
The border guards watch day and night, and they carry guns In a house in the village, a man and a woman are talking.

00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:51.415
The woman holds a six month old baby boy in her arms.

00:01:51.475 --> 00:01:57.938
She is excited, but she is afraid too.

00:01:57.998 --> 00:02:02.408
Tell me again, she says.

00:02:02.468 --> 00:02:07.017
Did he get to Austria all right last night?

00:02:07.077 --> 00:02:11.537
Yes, he did, the man says.

00:02:11.596 --> 00:02:13.848
Nobody saw him.

00:02:13.908 --> 00:02:16.160
Nobody heard him.

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:22.466
But last night was easy, because the sky was dark.

00:02:22.526 --> 00:02:26.078
Tonight, it's more difficult.

00:02:26.138 --> 00:02:29.331
Look at that moon.

00:02:29.391 --> 00:02:34.240
But it's Christmas night, the woman says.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:38.866
And the guards are drinking in the guardhouse, yes?

00:02:38.926 --> 00:02:42.767
That's true, says the man.

00:02:42.827 --> 00:02:49.258
But sometimes they come out and drive up and down the road for a time.

00:02:49.318 --> 00:02:51.969
So you must be careful.

00:02:52.029 --> 00:02:56.720
And you must run fast, very fast.

00:02:56.780 --> 00:02:59.690
He looks at his watch.

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:02.626
It's time to go.

00:03:02.686 --> 00:03:08.704
The woman puts on a white coat and a white hat.

00:03:08.764 --> 00:03:12.817
The baby wears a white coat too.

00:03:12.876 --> 00:03:16.990
And the woman carries him on her back.

00:03:17.050 --> 00:03:20.592
Good, the man says.

00:03:20.652 --> 00:03:23.904
White is best when there's snow.

00:03:23.964 --> 00:03:26.326
Nobody can see you.

00:03:26.385 --> 00:03:29.098
Now, are you ready?

00:03:29.158 --> 00:03:31.153
Let's go.

00:03:31.213 --> 00:03:37.581
They leave the house and walk quickly out of the village.

00:03:37.641 --> 00:03:47.067
After a time they stop and the man says very quietly, okay.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.898
Do you see those trees?

00:03:49.958 --> 00:03:55.142
Turn right there and go 50 meters.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:59.666
When you come to the road, go across it quickly.

00:03:59.726 --> 00:04:02.979
and run down the hill through the trees.

00:04:03.039 --> 00:04:05.810
Then you come to the river.

00:04:05.870 --> 00:04:11.051
Turn left and go 500 metres.

00:04:11.111 --> 00:04:17.413
The trees finish there and you can walk through the river easily.

00:04:17.473 --> 00:04:22.144
Across two more fields and you're in Austria.

00:04:22.204 --> 00:04:26.375
Our friends are waiting for you in the second field.

00:04:26.435 --> 00:04:28.176
Go now.

00:04:28.236 --> 00:04:29.920
Goodbye.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:31.946
good luck.

00:04:32.006 --> 00:04:35.189
The woman begins to run.

00:04:35.248 --> 00:04:38.632
The baby on her back is sleeping.

00:04:38.692 --> 00:04:44.486
But now he opens his eyes and begins to cry.

00:04:44.546 --> 00:04:49.300
The woman is afraid and runs more slowly.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:53.744
But the baby's crying is loud in the night.

00:04:53.804 --> 00:05:01.950
At the trees, the woman turns right and soon she is at the road.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:11.237
She does not see the black car under the trees, but the men in the car see her.

00:05:11.296 --> 00:05:17.691
Suddenly there is a noise in the night, the noise of guns.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.002
Then it is quiet again.

00:05:21.062 --> 00:05:26.026
The woman's body lies in the snow on the road.

00:05:26.086 --> 00:05:31.364
Now the only sound is the crying of the baby.

00:05:31.384 --> 00:05:38.978
Chapter 2 England 1995 Hey!

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:39.959
Jan!

00:05:40.019 --> 00:05:50.463
Look at this!

00:05:50.523 --> 00:06:00.586
Carol said.

00:06:00.646 --> 00:06:08.269
She had a letter in her hand and took it across to her husband at the breakfast table.

00:06:08.329 --> 00:06:12.790
It's from the Oxford Orchestra, she said.

00:06:12.850 --> 00:06:17.552
They're giving concerts in the Czech Republic this Christmas.

00:06:17.612 --> 00:06:30.514
They're doing three concerts in Prague and they're asking me to go because they need a harpist Shall we go to Prague for Christmas?

00:06:30.574 --> 00:06:36.346
I can play with the orchestra and you can come with us.

00:06:36.406 --> 00:06:39.108
When are the concerts?

00:06:39.168 --> 00:06:40.999
asked Jan.

00:06:41.058 --> 00:06:45.891
I always have a lot of work in the weeks before Christmas.

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:50.312
I must finish writing my new book then.

00:06:50.372 --> 00:06:55.027
Jan taught Czech at Oxford University.

00:06:55.087 --> 00:06:58.412
and wrote books about languages.

00:06:58.472 --> 00:07:07.599
He was born in Czechoslovakia, but came to England with his father when he was very young.

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:13.684
He met Carol when she was one of his students at university.

00:07:13.744 --> 00:07:19.138
The first concert is on December the 20th.

00:07:19.198 --> 00:07:23.728
Carol answered, are you free then?

00:07:23.788 --> 00:07:27.747
No, I'm sorry, Carol.

00:07:27.807 --> 00:07:29.468
Jan said.

00:07:29.528 --> 00:07:34.261
But I can't come before December the 24th.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.713
Well, it doesn't matter.

00:07:37.772 --> 00:07:41.154
You can come for the second concert.

00:07:41.214 --> 00:07:44.677
It's on December the 25th.

00:07:44.736 --> 00:07:47.928
But what about my father?

00:07:47.988 --> 00:07:49.679
Said Jan.

00:07:49.739 --> 00:07:53.832
We can't go away and leave him at Christmas time.

00:07:53.892 --> 00:07:57.222
He loves a family Christmas with us.

00:07:57.282 --> 00:07:59.943
You know that.

00:08:00.003 --> 00:08:08.644
Josef Flak was 68 years old, and his eyes were bad.

00:08:08.704 --> 00:08:12.255
He couldn't see very well.

00:08:12.315 --> 00:08:16.386
So he lived with Carol and Jan.

00:08:16.446 --> 00:08:20.027
Josef can come with us.

00:08:20.087 --> 00:08:22.126
Carol said.

00:08:22.186 --> 00:08:26.588
He often talks about Prague at Christmas.

00:08:26.648 --> 00:08:36.263
He says it's the most beautiful time of the year there, because of all the snow on the old buildings.

00:08:36.322 --> 00:08:43.677
I know, said Jan, but he only talks about Prague.

00:08:43.737 --> 00:08:46.890
He never wants to go there.

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:52.411
Every time we ask him to come with us, he says no.

00:08:52.471 --> 00:08:58.454
I don't know why, but I think it's because of my mother.

00:08:58.514 --> 00:09:04.378
When he thinks about Prague, he remembers her.

00:09:04.438 --> 00:09:14.396
You know, sometimes he cries when he looks at his photo of her after all these years.

00:09:14.456 --> 00:09:23.337
Just then, the door opened and Jan's father came slowly into the room.

00:09:23.397 --> 00:09:29.914
Good morning, he said, and sat down at the table.

00:09:29.974 --> 00:09:32.675
Is there any coffee?

00:09:32.735 --> 00:09:37.366
It's cold now, said Carol.

00:09:37.426 --> 00:09:40.388
Shall I make you some more?

00:09:40.448 --> 00:09:42.909
Thank you, my dear.

00:09:42.969 --> 00:09:48.040
He answered, you're very good to me.

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.522
Carol went out for some coffee.

00:09:52.582 --> 00:09:56.962
Jan looked at his father carefully.

00:09:57.022 --> 00:10:05.526
I must ask him now, he thought, while Carol is out of the room.

00:10:05.586 --> 00:10:11.037
You're very quiet, Jan, said the old man.

00:10:11.057 --> 00:10:14.288
Is something wrong?

00:10:14.348 --> 00:10:19.000
No, no, said Jan quickly.

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:21.320
Nothing's wrong.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:32.220
It's just I want to ask you a question, but it's difficult.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:34.860
Jan stopped.

00:10:34.921 --> 00:10:37.792
His father smiled.

00:10:37.853 --> 00:10:40.094
Difficult?

00:10:40.154 --> 00:10:42.905
Why is it difficult?

00:10:42.965 --> 00:10:46.737
Are you afraid of an old man?

00:10:46.797 --> 00:10:51.267
Of course not, said Jan.

00:10:51.327 --> 00:10:55.766
but I am afraid of your answer.

00:10:55.826 --> 00:11:01.158
You see, Carol wants to go very much.

00:11:01.218 --> 00:11:07.329
She loves playing her harp, but it's Christmas time and...

00:11:07.389 --> 00:11:08.870
stop!

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:10.470
said Joseph.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:13.361
What are you talking about?

00:11:13.421 --> 00:11:17.552
Where does Carol want to go at Christmas?

00:11:17.612 --> 00:11:19.803
To Prague!

00:11:19.863 --> 00:11:21.482
said Jan.

00:11:21.542 --> 00:11:25.054
and I would like to go with her.

00:11:25.114 --> 00:11:28.856
We want you to come too."

00:11:28.916 --> 00:11:30.896
Ah!

00:11:30.956 --> 00:11:32.988
said the old man.

00:11:33.048 --> 00:11:35.340
To Prague.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.751
I understand now.

00:11:38.811 --> 00:11:43.294
The room was suddenly very quiet.

00:11:43.354 --> 00:11:48.876
Jan drank his cold coffee and waited.

00:11:48.936 --> 00:11:54.160
The old man took something out of his pocket.

00:11:54.220 --> 00:12:00.752
It was a photograph of his dead wife, Jan's mother.

00:12:00.812 --> 00:12:10.058
He spoke very quietly, not to Jan, but to the photograph in his hand.

00:12:10.118 --> 00:12:20.421
Perhaps now, before I die, just once I can go back again.

00:12:20.481 --> 00:12:25.012
Carol came back with some hot coffee.

00:12:25.072 --> 00:12:29.685
She looked at Joseph, then at Jan.

00:12:29.745 --> 00:12:31.696
Shh.

00:12:31.756 --> 00:12:34.608
He's thinking about Prague.

00:12:34.668 --> 00:12:37.630
Jan said quietly.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:43.374
Carol put the coffee on the table and sat down.

00:12:43.434 --> 00:12:49.980
The hands on the clock slowly moved through two long minutes.

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:55.934
Then the old man put the photograph back in his pocket.

00:12:55.994 --> 00:12:59.666
All right, he said.

00:12:59.726 --> 00:13:03.587
Let's all go to Prague for Christmas.

00:13:03.647 --> 00:13:07.178
It's beautiful there when it snows.

00:13:07.238 --> 00:13:10.040
I remember it so well.

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:19.364
So very well.

00:13:19.424 --> 00:13:40.229
Chapter 3 The Accident The first rehearsal began at nine o'clock and finished at two o'clock.

00:13:40.289 --> 00:13:46.059
What a long morning, everyone said.

00:13:46.119 --> 00:13:53.319
I'm sorry," said the conductor, but we have very little time.

00:13:53.379 --> 00:14:00.520
The first concert is tomorrow night, and a lot of important people are coming.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.651
So we must play well.

00:14:03.711 --> 00:14:07.642
Now, please go and eat.

00:14:07.702 --> 00:14:10.982
This afternoon is free.

00:14:11.042 --> 00:14:15.820
So you can go and look at this beautiful city.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:21.170
Tomorrow morning we begin again at nine o'clock.

00:14:21.230 --> 00:14:25.213
Please don't be late.

00:14:25.273 --> 00:14:33.178
Carol left the rehearsal room with Alan, one of the first violinists.

00:14:33.238 --> 00:14:37.632
What are you going to do this afternoon, Carol?

00:14:37.692 --> 00:14:39.592
Alan asked.

00:14:39.652 --> 00:14:47.348
I'm going to get a quick sandwich And then I'm going shopping," Carol said.

00:14:47.408 --> 00:14:53.502
My husband, Jan, and his father are arriving on Sunday.

00:14:53.562 --> 00:15:00.134
Monday is Christmas day, and I haven't got any presents for them.

00:15:00.195 --> 00:15:06.821
I must find something this afternoon, only free afternoon.

00:15:06.881 --> 00:15:11.756
See you tomorrow, then," said Alan.

00:15:11.816 --> 00:15:15.237
And, good luck with the shopping.

00:15:15.297 --> 00:15:19.008
Thanks, Carol said.

00:15:19.068 --> 00:15:29.300
There are some wonderful shops in the Stade Mesto, the old town, so I'm going down there.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:35.082
Carol went into a lot of shops that afternoon.

00:15:35.142 --> 00:15:43.394
In the end, She got a book for Jan and a picture for his father.

00:15:43.454 --> 00:15:49.616
When she left the old town, it was nearly dark.

00:15:49.676 --> 00:15:58.650
It was very cold, so she walked quickly through the streets, back to her hotel.

00:15:58.710 --> 00:16:06.867
There were Christmas trees in all the shop windows, and the city looked beautiful.

00:16:06.927 --> 00:16:10.344
There was a lot of noise, too.

00:16:10.404 --> 00:16:16.568
People, cars, taxis, buses.

00:16:16.628 --> 00:16:22.862
Everybody's doing their Christmas shopping, Carol thought.

00:16:22.922 --> 00:16:28.606
Suddenly, she saw a man across the street.

00:16:28.666 --> 00:16:31.028
It was Jan.

00:16:31.088 --> 00:16:34.029
Why was he in Prague so soon?

00:16:34.049 --> 00:16:35.900
Jan?

00:16:35.960 --> 00:16:40.082
She shouted across the street.

00:16:40.142 --> 00:16:43.244
But Jan didn't hear her.

00:16:43.304 --> 00:16:45.474
He walked on.

00:16:45.534 --> 00:16:50.018
Carol shouted again, very loudly.

00:16:50.078 --> 00:16:51.708
Jan?

00:16:51.768 --> 00:16:53.340
Jan?

00:16:53.400 --> 00:16:56.582
It's me, Carol!

00:16:56.642 --> 00:17:00.764
A lot of people stopped this time.

00:17:00.824 --> 00:17:03.926
They all looked at her.

00:17:03.986 --> 00:17:07.113
The man stopped too.

00:17:07.173 --> 00:17:16.824
He turned and looked at Carol for a minute, but he didn't smile and he didn't speak.

00:17:16.884 --> 00:17:21.137
It was a very long minute for Carol.

00:17:21.197 --> 00:17:29.172
Her husband's eyes were cold and Carol began to feel afraid.

00:17:29.232 --> 00:17:41.982
Then he moved and began to walk away from Carol down a little street Carol did not understand it.

00:17:42.042 --> 00:17:44.623
But she knew one thing.

00:17:44.683 --> 00:17:48.204
She did not want to lose him.

00:17:48.264 --> 00:17:52.286
Perhaps he didn't see me very well.

00:17:52.346 --> 00:17:54.877
It's so dark now.

00:17:54.937 --> 00:17:56.838
He's going.

00:17:56.898 --> 00:17:59.249
Where is he going?

00:17:59.309 --> 00:18:00.680
Jan?

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:02.130
Come back?

00:18:02.190 --> 00:18:04.351
Are you ill?

00:18:04.411 --> 00:18:07.656
She ran across the street.

00:18:07.716 --> 00:18:12.862
There was a sudden noise, and somebody shouted.

00:18:12.923 --> 00:18:18.756
Two seconds later, Carol lay in the snow.

00:18:18.816 --> 00:18:25.208
She ran right in front of me, the bus driver said later.

00:18:25.268 --> 00:18:27.328
I couldn't stop.

00:18:27.388 --> 00:18:30.120
There was no time.

00:18:30.180 --> 00:18:36.926
Carol's face was white, and her eyes were closed.

00:18:36.986 --> 00:18:43.052
Soon an ambulance came and took her body away.

00:18:43.112 --> 00:18:48.564
Was she alive or dead?

00:18:48.624 --> 00:18:56.476
At nine o'clock the next morning the conductor was ready to begin the rehearsal.

00:18:56.536 --> 00:19:02.928
He opened his music and the orchestra started to play.

00:19:02.988 --> 00:19:11.038
Suddenly his hands stopped moving and the music stopped at once.

00:19:11.098 --> 00:19:13.320
Harpist?

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.402
The conductor shouted angrily.

00:19:16.462 --> 00:19:18.754
What's the matter with you?

00:19:18.814 --> 00:19:20.695
Are you sleeping?

00:19:20.755 --> 00:19:23.908
You begin to play here.

00:19:23.968 --> 00:19:27.870
Excuse me, Mr. Renaldi?

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:30.764
Said someone at the back of the room.

00:19:30.824 --> 00:19:34.224
The harpist is not here.

00:19:34.284 --> 00:19:40.896
Everyone turned and looked at the harp at the back of the orchestra.

00:19:40.956 --> 00:19:43.248
It was true.

00:19:43.308 --> 00:19:47.420
There was nobody in the harpist's chair.

00:19:47.480 --> 00:19:51.142
Well, where is she?

00:19:51.202 --> 00:19:53.442
asked the conductor.

00:19:53.502 --> 00:19:56.174
There was no answer.

00:19:56.234 --> 00:19:59.136
We can't wait for her.

00:19:59.196 --> 00:20:04.473
He said, we must have this rehearsal without her.

00:20:04.533 --> 00:20:06.498
Where is Alan?

00:20:06.558 --> 00:20:09.319
He can speak some check.

00:20:09.379 --> 00:20:12.219
Alan stood up.

00:20:12.279 --> 00:20:17.270
Can you go to the hotel and look for her there?

00:20:17.330 --> 00:20:19.521
The conductor asked.

00:20:19.581 --> 00:20:25.732
Then come back here at once, with or without her.

00:20:25.792 --> 00:20:28.472
Alan left.

00:20:28.532 --> 00:20:33.016
Half an hour later, he was back.

00:20:33.076 --> 00:20:37.521
She's not at the hotel, he said.

00:20:37.581 --> 00:20:46.924
I spoke to two or three people in the hotel, and they say that Carol wasn't there at breakfast this morning.

00:20:46.984 --> 00:20:53.056
And they think that she didn't sleep in her room last night.

00:20:53.116 --> 00:20:58.157
I don't like this, said the conductor.

00:20:58.217 --> 00:21:01.696
Carol is never late for rehearsals.

00:21:01.756 --> 00:21:06.938
And she knows that these concerts are important for us.

00:21:06.998 --> 00:21:10.720
I think we must tell the police.

00:21:10.780 --> 00:21:13.481
Shall I do it now?

00:21:13.541 --> 00:21:15.302
Alan asked.

00:21:15.362 --> 00:21:18.314
Yes, said the conductor.

00:21:18.374 --> 00:21:27.208
Please go now.

00:21:27.268 --> 00:21:40.804
Chapter 4 Nobody understands Carol.

00:21:40.865 --> 00:21:45.445
Carol slowly opened her eyes.

00:21:45.505 --> 00:21:48.536
Her head hurt.

00:21:48.596 --> 00:21:51.776
She closed her eyes again.

00:21:51.836 --> 00:21:55.057
A man said something.

00:21:55.117 --> 00:21:57.578
What was it?

00:21:57.638 --> 00:21:59.848
Carol!

00:21:59.908 --> 00:22:01.619
She heard.

00:22:01.679 --> 00:22:03.304
Carol!

00:22:03.364 --> 00:22:04.898
Can you hear me?

00:22:04.918 --> 00:22:10.991
I can hear you, Carol said.

00:22:11.051 --> 00:22:15.212
But I don't want to open my eyes.

00:22:15.272 --> 00:22:18.284
My head hurts.

00:22:18.344 --> 00:22:21.165
Who are you?

00:22:21.226 --> 00:22:30.068
It's me, Georgiore Naldi, the conductor of the orchestra.

00:22:30.128 --> 00:22:33.292
Mr. Naldi?

00:22:33.352 --> 00:22:36.794
Carol opened her eyes again.

00:22:36.854 --> 00:22:41.244
Her head didn't hurt so much this time.

00:22:41.304 --> 00:22:44.825
What are you doing in my bedroom?

00:22:44.885 --> 00:22:46.866
She asked angrily.

00:22:46.926 --> 00:22:49.216
What's happening?

00:22:49.276 --> 00:22:52.657
This isn't your bedroom.

00:22:52.717 --> 00:22:55.088
Said Mr. Analdi.

00:22:55.148 --> 00:22:58.768
It's a hospital in Prague.

00:22:58.828 --> 00:23:02.156
You had an accident yesterday.

00:23:02.216 --> 00:23:06.613
Can you remember anything about it?

00:23:06.673 --> 00:23:10.944
Suddenly Carol remembered everything.

00:23:11.004 --> 00:23:18.476
The old town, the Christmas trees in the shop windows, Christmas presents.

00:23:18.536 --> 00:23:20.176
Jan!

00:23:20.236 --> 00:23:22.036
Jan!

00:23:22.096 --> 00:23:24.247
She sat up.

00:23:24.307 --> 00:23:26.127
Jan!

00:23:26.187 --> 00:23:27.878
Where's Jan?

00:23:27.938 --> 00:23:30.386
She asked Mr. Enaldi.

00:23:30.446 --> 00:23:34.976
Please, Mrs. Black, said a woman quietly.

00:23:35.036 --> 00:23:37.148
Don't get excited.

00:23:37.208 --> 00:23:39.480
Lie down again.

00:23:39.540 --> 00:23:42.622
Carol turned her head.

00:23:42.682 --> 00:23:45.312
It hurt again.

00:23:45.372 --> 00:23:51.646
Near the door of the room, she saw a woman in a white coat.

00:23:51.706 --> 00:23:53.978
A doctor.

00:23:54.038 --> 00:23:57.230
But I must see Jan.

00:23:57.290 --> 00:24:00.728
Carol said, where is he?

00:24:00.788 --> 00:24:02.344
I must find him.

00:24:02.364 --> 00:24:03.945
I can't.

00:24:04.005 --> 00:24:05.676
Oh, dear.

00:24:05.736 --> 00:24:08.798
She put her hand her head.

00:24:08.858 --> 00:24:11.010
Who's Jan?

00:24:11.070 --> 00:24:14.582
The doctor asked Mr. Inaldi quietly.

00:24:14.642 --> 00:24:18.414
Her husband, he answered.

00:24:18.474 --> 00:24:21.676
He took Carol's hand.

00:24:21.736 --> 00:24:23.438
Listen.

00:24:23.498 --> 00:24:26.420
Your husband is coming.

00:24:26.480 --> 00:24:29.822
We told him about the accident.

00:24:29.882 --> 00:24:33.852
He's on a plane from London now.

00:24:33.912 --> 00:24:36.503
On a plane?

00:24:36.563 --> 00:24:37.683
Why?

00:24:37.703 --> 00:24:41.004
He's here in Prague.

00:24:41.064 --> 00:24:45.045
I saw him in the street near the Old Town.

00:24:45.065 --> 00:24:52.486
I called out to him and he saw me, but he didn't stop.

00:24:52.547 --> 00:24:56.577
He just walked away from me.

00:24:56.637 --> 00:24:58.798
Please find him.

00:24:58.858 --> 00:25:00.059
Please.

00:25:00.119 --> 00:25:01.710
I must talk to him.

00:25:01.730 --> 00:25:03.821
I must."

00:25:03.881 --> 00:25:08.112
The doctor moved nearer to the bed.

00:25:08.172 --> 00:25:12.153
Yann is coming soon, Mrs. Blach.

00:25:12.213 --> 00:25:16.274
She said, please don't get excited.

00:25:16.334 --> 00:25:18.695
It's not good for you.

00:25:18.755 --> 00:25:24.478
Now, lie down again and close your eyes.

00:25:24.538 --> 00:25:26.958
You must sleep.

00:25:27.018 --> 00:25:31.420
And I know you're feeling very tired.

00:25:31.481 --> 00:25:36.564
Carol lay down and closed her eyes.

00:25:36.624 --> 00:25:39.324
The doctor was right.

00:25:39.384 --> 00:25:42.186
She was tired.

00:25:42.246 --> 00:25:45.598
But why didn't they listen?

00:25:45.658 --> 00:25:48.610
Why didn't they understand?

00:25:48.670 --> 00:25:53.672
Jan was in Prague, and she must find him.

00:25:53.732 --> 00:25:56.054
Talk to him.

00:25:56.114 --> 00:26:02.596
The doctor looked at Mr. Inaldi and spoke very quietly.

00:26:02.656 --> 00:26:06.058
Let's leave her now, please.

00:26:06.118 --> 00:26:08.489
She needs to sleep.

00:26:08.549 --> 00:26:12.120
You can come back later.

00:26:12.181 --> 00:26:17.699
Mr. Inaldi and the doctor left the room.

00:26:17.759 --> 00:26:26.076
They closed the door quietly, and then looked at Carol through the window in the door.

00:26:26.136 --> 00:26:31.328
She's going to be all right, said the doctor.

00:26:31.388 --> 00:26:34.818
She just needs to sleep for a time.

00:26:34.878 --> 00:26:37.628
There's nothing wrong with her.

00:26:37.688 --> 00:26:42.339
Yes, there is, said Mr. Inaudi.

00:26:42.400 --> 00:26:45.659
She thinks her husband is in Prague.

00:26:45.719 --> 00:26:53.190
But I spoke to him on the telephone three hours ago, and he was in Oxford.

00:26:53.250 --> 00:26:58.331
I'm afraid she's ill, very ill.

00:26:58.391 --> 00:27:01.912
Listen, said the doctor.

00:27:01.972 --> 00:27:12.966
She had a bad hit on the head in the accident, but she didn't break anything, and her head is all right.

00:27:13.026 --> 00:27:16.950
We looked at it very carefully.

00:27:17.010 --> 00:27:22.624
She's going to be okay after a good sleep.

00:27:22.684 --> 00:27:31.240
But all this talk about Jan, her husband, said Mr. Inaldi.

00:27:31.300 --> 00:27:33.712
What about that?

00:27:33.772 --> 00:27:38.085
Yes, she's confused about that.

00:27:38.145 --> 00:27:39.686
It's true.

00:27:39.746 --> 00:27:42.828
But she remembers her name.

00:27:42.888 --> 00:27:50.032
She knows you, and she understands that she's in hospital.

00:27:50.092 --> 00:27:53.254
All this is very good.

00:27:53.314 --> 00:27:58.596
Now, what about you, Mr. Analdi?

00:27:58.656 --> 00:28:04.549
It's a difficult time for you, too, because of your concerts.

00:28:04.610 --> 00:28:06.800
I understand that.

00:28:06.860 --> 00:28:10.432
But please go away now.

00:28:10.492 --> 00:28:12.212
Eat something.

00:28:12.272 --> 00:28:17.414
have a sleep, then come back later this afternoon.

00:28:17.474 --> 00:28:21.186
You can't do anything now."

00:28:21.246 --> 00:28:25.370
All right, said Mr. Enaldi.

00:28:25.430 --> 00:28:28.252
But he was not happy.

00:28:28.312 --> 00:28:32.006
Poor Carol, he thought.

00:28:32.066 --> 00:28:42.200
And my poor orchestra, how can I find another harpist before tonight's concert?

00:28:42.260 --> 00:29:02.437
Chapter 5 Some visitors for Carol Two hours later, a tall man arrived at the hospital.

00:29:02.497 --> 00:29:14.623
He asked to see the woman in yesterday's street accident.

00:29:14.683 --> 00:29:17.934
He didn't know her name.

00:29:17.994 --> 00:29:21.945
The doctor came downstairs.

00:29:22.005 --> 00:29:24.946
Who are you?

00:29:25.006 --> 00:29:27.806
She asked the man.

00:29:27.866 --> 00:29:32.168
My name is Pavel Brechter.

00:29:32.228 --> 00:29:40.448
I saw the accident and I called the ambulance Is the woman all right?

00:29:40.508 --> 00:29:43.708
I just wanted to know that.

00:29:43.768 --> 00:29:47.439
I was afraid she was dead.

00:29:47.499 --> 00:29:50.720
The doctor smiled.

00:29:50.780 --> 00:29:53.820
Would you like to see her?

00:29:53.880 --> 00:29:56.852
She's much better now.

00:29:56.912 --> 00:29:59.232
Yes, please.

00:29:59.292 --> 00:30:01.402
Answer, Pavel.

00:30:01.462 --> 00:30:04.343
Then come with me.

00:30:04.403 --> 00:30:08.063
They went upstairs in the lift.

00:30:08.123 --> 00:30:11.854
and walked along to Carol's room.

00:30:11.914 --> 00:30:18.708
At the door they stopped and looked in through the window.

00:30:18.768 --> 00:30:23.620
She's sleeping, said the doctor.

00:30:23.680 --> 00:30:28.864
But she looks well, said Pavel.

00:30:28.924 --> 00:30:32.856
Yesterday she looked so white.

00:30:32.916 --> 00:30:36.452
I was afraid for her.

00:30:36.512 --> 00:30:46.292
Just then Carol opened her eyes and saw a man through the window in her door.

00:30:46.352 --> 00:30:48.702
She sat up.

00:30:48.762 --> 00:30:50.463
Jan!

00:30:50.523 --> 00:30:52.164
She shouted.

00:30:52.224 --> 00:30:54.125
Jan!

00:30:54.185 --> 00:30:56.336
Oh dear!

00:30:56.396 --> 00:31:00.768
The doctor said, not again.

00:31:00.828 --> 00:31:08.336
She hit her head in the accident And she's confused about some things.

00:31:08.396 --> 00:31:14.038
She thinks that you are her husband from England.

00:31:14.098 --> 00:31:16.350
Shall I go?

00:31:16.410 --> 00:31:18.221
asked Parvel.

00:31:18.281 --> 00:31:20.622
Perhaps it's better.

00:31:20.682 --> 00:31:24.554
Yes, answered the doctor.

00:31:24.615 --> 00:31:29.948
She went into Carol's room and closed the door.

00:31:30.008 --> 00:31:34.443
Parvel walked slowly back to the lift.

00:31:34.504 --> 00:31:44.301
Then the lift door opened and a man ran out with some beautiful red flowers in his arms.

00:31:44.361 --> 00:31:51.683
He looked at the numbers of the rooms and then went quickly into Carol's room.

00:31:51.743 --> 00:31:59.826
He didn't see Parvel, but an older man came slowly out of the lift next.

00:31:59.886 --> 00:32:04.622
He saw Parvel and stopped suddenly.

00:32:04.683 --> 00:32:08.088
Pavel stopped too.

00:32:08.148 --> 00:32:13.110
I'm sorry, said the old man.

00:32:13.170 --> 00:32:16.800
My eyes aren't very good.

00:32:16.860 --> 00:32:18.811
I thought...

00:32:18.871 --> 00:32:22.192
you see, you look.

00:32:22.252 --> 00:32:26.662
Yes, I know, said Pavel.

00:32:26.722 --> 00:32:29.423
I saw your friend.

00:32:29.483 --> 00:32:32.464
He's not my friend.

00:32:32.524 --> 00:32:34.737
He's my son.

00:32:34.797 --> 00:32:40.594
Please, tell me, what is your name?

00:32:40.654 --> 00:32:43.746
Parvel Brichter.

00:32:43.806 --> 00:32:47.649
The old man looked very afraid.

00:32:47.709 --> 00:32:53.544
His face went white, and his mouth opened and closed.

00:32:53.604 --> 00:32:56.145
But he said nothing.

00:32:56.206 --> 00:33:00.038
Now Parvel was afraid.

00:33:00.098 --> 00:33:04.386
You don't look very well, he said.

00:33:04.446 --> 00:33:06.552
Would you like to sit down?

00:33:06.572 --> 00:33:09.543
And shall I call a doctor?

00:33:09.603 --> 00:33:12.794
There's a doctor in this room here.

00:33:12.854 --> 00:33:16.755
Please, said the old man.

00:33:16.815 --> 00:33:20.376
My son is in that room.

00:33:20.436 --> 00:33:23.717
Please take me to him.

00:33:23.777 --> 00:33:28.924
Pavel took the old man's arm.

00:33:28.984 --> 00:33:38.102
In Carol's room, Jan put the red flowers on the bed and took his wife's hands.

00:33:38.163 --> 00:33:40.484
Oh, my love.

00:33:40.544 --> 00:33:42.184
Are you all right?

00:33:42.244 --> 00:33:46.576
He said, I can't understand it.

00:33:46.636 --> 00:33:49.917
Why did you run in front of a bus?

00:33:49.977 --> 00:33:52.448
How did it happen?

00:33:52.508 --> 00:33:56.840
Carol didn't answer his questions.

00:33:56.900 --> 00:33:59.116
Jan?

00:33:59.176 --> 00:34:02.243
She looked up into his face.

00:34:02.303 --> 00:34:04.694
You are Jan.

00:34:04.754 --> 00:34:07.294
Tell me that you're Jan.

00:34:07.355 --> 00:34:10.195
Of course I'm Jan.

00:34:10.256 --> 00:34:13.307
What are you talking about?

00:34:13.366 --> 00:34:17.127
The doctor came up to the bed.

00:34:17.188 --> 00:34:21.014
Wait a minute, she said.

00:34:21.074 --> 00:34:26.290
You told me that your name was Parvo Brister.

00:34:26.350 --> 00:34:31.512
Are you Mrs. Black's husband or not?

00:34:31.573 --> 00:34:37.145
Just then, Carol looked behind Jan.

00:34:37.206 --> 00:34:44.038
She saw Parvo with Jan's father through the window of her door.

00:34:44.098 --> 00:34:49.456
Her eyes got bigger and bigger.

00:34:49.517 --> 00:34:55.204
Is that, she said.

00:34:55.264 --> 00:35:00.866
Jan and the doctor turned and saw Parvel.

00:35:00.926 --> 00:35:05.688
My God, said Jan.

00:35:05.748 --> 00:35:08.368
I don't know.

00:35:08.428 --> 00:35:12.760
The doctor looked back at Jan's face.

00:35:12.820 --> 00:35:21.207
Two men, but only one face, she said quietly.

00:35:21.267 --> 00:35:29.994
Then Jan's father opened the door of Carol's room, and the two men came in.

00:35:30.054 --> 00:35:32.986
Jan stood up.

00:35:33.046 --> 00:35:36.036
He looked at his father.

00:35:36.096 --> 00:35:39.257
Who is this man?

00:35:39.317 --> 00:35:41.488
He asked.

00:35:41.548 --> 00:35:48.466
His name is Parvo Brichter, answered his father.

00:35:48.526 --> 00:35:53.665
Please, bring me a chair and some water.

00:35:53.725 --> 00:35:59.450
I need to sit down before I can answer your question.

00:35:59.511 --> 00:36:06.447
Jan got a chair for his father and the doctor gave him some water.

00:36:06.507 --> 00:36:18.118
Then she left the room quietly.

00:36:18.178 --> 00:36:30.640
Chapter 6 Who is Parva?

00:36:30.700 --> 00:36:36.134
The old man drank some water and looked up.

00:36:36.194 --> 00:36:44.435
Parva, he said, I must ask you to look at this photo.

00:36:44.495 --> 00:36:53.131
He put his hand in his pocket and took out a photograph of a young woman.

00:36:53.191 --> 00:36:57.832
Do you know this woman?

00:36:57.892 --> 00:37:01.693
Yes, said Pavel.

00:37:01.753 --> 00:37:06.564
That's a photo of my mother, Lenka.

00:37:06.624 --> 00:37:10.259
She died when I was very young.

00:37:10.319 --> 00:37:18.057
But my grandmother had many photos of her, and we often looked at them.

00:37:18.117 --> 00:37:24.782
Did you live with your grandmother when you were young?

00:37:24.842 --> 00:37:26.472
Yes, I did.

00:37:26.492 --> 00:37:31.426
But how do you know all this?

00:37:31.486 --> 00:37:40.268
Because, said Joseph, Lenka was my wife.

00:37:40.328 --> 00:37:42.456
Dad?

00:37:42.516 --> 00:37:44.227
What are you saying?

00:37:44.287 --> 00:37:46.218
Said Yan.

00:37:46.278 --> 00:37:49.518
You're as if looked at Yan.

00:37:49.578 --> 00:37:51.849
My boy.

00:37:51.909 --> 00:37:55.260
Don't be angry with me.

00:37:55.321 --> 00:38:00.982
I didn't tell you many things about your mother.

00:38:01.042 --> 00:38:04.183
Perhaps I was wrong.

00:38:04.243 --> 00:38:07.794
But I wanted to forget.

00:38:07.854 --> 00:38:11.270
Not to forget your mother.

00:38:11.330 --> 00:38:18.208
only to forget that terrible night in 1957.

00:38:18.268 --> 00:38:26.181
Jan, this man, Parvel, is your twin brother.

00:38:26.242 --> 00:38:29.673
You can see that it's true.

00:38:29.733 --> 00:38:33.264
Look at your faces.

00:38:33.324 --> 00:38:43.332
Parvel looked at Jan, So I have a brother, he said.

00:38:43.392 --> 00:38:47.465
My grandmother never told me that.

00:38:47.525 --> 00:38:50.658
Jan smiled.

00:38:50.718 --> 00:38:59.895
And my father, our father, never told me about a twin brother.

00:38:59.955 --> 00:39:02.506
He turned to Joseph.

00:39:02.567 --> 00:39:07.168
Tards, why didn't you tell me?

00:39:07.228 --> 00:39:12.908
It's a long story," said the old man.

00:39:12.968 --> 00:39:21.460
It begins many years ago when a young man went to Prague University.

00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:31.392
He was there for seven years, and in his last year he met a beautiful young woman.

00:39:31.453 --> 00:39:39.351
His eyes turned to the photo She was so beautiful.

00:39:39.412 --> 00:39:49.257
Of course, the young man fell in love with her, and they got married in 1956.

00:39:49.318 --> 00:39:53.190
But things were difficult in Prague then.

00:39:53.250 --> 00:39:58.562
People were not happy, and they were not free.

00:39:58.622 --> 00:40:10.004
Lenke and I, and a lot of our friends, wanted to change things, but it was dangerous work.

00:40:10.064 --> 00:40:16.366
The Russians knew about us, and they watched us all the time.

00:40:16.426 --> 00:40:26.598
Then you two boys were born on a wonderful day in June 1957.

00:40:26.658 --> 00:40:31.475
But you went away, Parvel said angrily.

00:40:31.535 --> 00:40:35.712
Your wife died and you left the country.

00:40:35.772 --> 00:40:41.103
You went away to England and began a new life.

00:40:41.163 --> 00:40:43.234
You didn't write.

00:40:43.294 --> 00:40:45.374
You didn't telephone.

00:40:45.434 --> 00:40:48.056
You weren't interested in me.

00:40:48.116 --> 00:40:50.306
Your son.

00:40:50.366 --> 00:40:54.678
Joseph's face was very sad.

00:40:54.738 --> 00:40:58.309
Power, he said.

00:40:58.369 --> 00:41:02.033
I thought you were dead.

00:41:02.093 --> 00:41:07.189
Look, I must show you something.

00:41:07.249 --> 00:41:16.187
From behind the photo of his wife, he took out a letter and gave it to Parval.

00:41:16.247 --> 00:41:20.460
The letter was old and yellow.

00:41:20.520 --> 00:41:26.195
Parval opened it and began to read.

00:41:26.255 --> 00:41:33.879
The letter was in check, and it was his grandmother's writing.

00:41:33.939 --> 00:41:40.970
I write to tell you, Joseph, that your wife is dead.

00:41:41.030 --> 00:41:48.704
On Christmas night, the guards shot her on the road at the border.

00:41:48.764 --> 00:42:02.580
She carried Parvel, your baby's son, and my grandson, on her back, and the guards shot him too.

00:42:02.640 --> 00:42:07.694
Your wife and your son are dead.

00:42:07.754 --> 00:42:14.149
Your friends came and told me yesterday.

00:42:14.209 --> 00:42:20.224
You have yarn and a new life in England.

00:42:20.284 --> 00:42:22.666
And what do I have?

00:42:22.726 --> 00:42:24.318
Nothing.

00:42:24.378 --> 00:42:36.766
You took one grandson away from me, and now my daughter and little Parval are dead because of you.

00:42:36.826 --> 00:42:43.080
Don't write to me, and don't come back to Prague.

00:42:43.140 --> 00:42:49.656
I never want to see you or hear from you again."

00:42:49.716 --> 00:42:53.139
Stanner's lover.

00:42:53.199 --> 00:42:59.319
Slowly Parval put the letter down.

00:42:59.379 --> 00:43:05.268
I understand now, he said quietly.

00:43:05.328 --> 00:43:08.640
What a terrible letter!

00:43:08.700 --> 00:43:11.592
How could she do that to you?

00:43:11.652 --> 00:43:14.003
And to me!

00:43:14.063 --> 00:43:19.426
Stanislava loved her daughter very much.

00:43:19.486 --> 00:43:21.978
Joseph said sadly.

00:43:22.038 --> 00:43:28.032
She loved you too, and didn't want to lose you.

00:43:28.092 --> 00:43:30.722
I see that now.

00:43:30.782 --> 00:43:33.922
But she never liked me.

00:43:33.982 --> 00:43:40.314
And after that letter, how could I go back to Prague?

00:43:40.374 --> 00:43:42.565
You were dead.

00:43:42.625 --> 00:43:44.986
Lenko was dead.

00:43:45.046 --> 00:43:48.737
He put his face in his hands.

00:43:48.797 --> 00:43:52.888
The room was very quiet.

00:43:52.948 --> 00:43:58.538
Then Parval put his hand on his father's arm.

00:43:58.598 --> 00:44:03.888
Stanner's lover is dead now, he said.

00:44:03.948 --> 00:44:07.560
You and I can begin again.

00:44:07.620 --> 00:44:14.634
He smiled and learned to be father and son.

00:44:14.694 --> 00:44:19.688
Joseph's face was wet with tears.

00:44:19.748 --> 00:44:26.232
He put his hand over Pavel's hand and smiled back at him.

00:44:26.292 --> 00:44:29.090
But he could not speak.

00:44:29.150 --> 00:44:34.289
Now there were tears in everybody's eyes.

00:44:34.349 --> 00:44:50.706
After a minute or two, Jan said, Dad, I know it's difficult for you, but can you tell us about that Christmas in 1957?

00:44:50.766 --> 00:44:53.618
How did it all happen?

00:44:53.678 --> 00:44:56.308
I'd like to know.

00:44:56.368 --> 00:45:00.209
Yes, said his father.

00:45:00.269 --> 00:45:04.960
You and Pavel must know.

00:45:05.020 --> 00:45:07.882
He turned to Pavel.

00:45:07.942 --> 00:45:12.914
But what did Stannis Lava tell you?

00:45:12.974 --> 00:45:16.766
Very little, Pavel said.

00:45:16.826 --> 00:45:20.278
She never wanted to talk about it.

00:45:20.338 --> 00:45:27.152
She told me that my mother died in hospital and you went away to England.

00:45:27.212 --> 00:45:29.396
That was all.

00:45:29.456 --> 00:45:34.282
I can understand that," said Joseph.

00:45:34.342 --> 00:45:37.263
Poor Stannis Lava.

00:45:37.323 --> 00:45:42.065
She lost her daughter because of me.

00:45:42.125 --> 00:45:46.626
And she never liked our work for freedom, you see.

00:45:46.687 --> 00:45:49.308
She didn't understand.

00:45:49.368 --> 00:45:53.990
She just wanted a quiet family life.

00:45:54.050 --> 00:45:58.732
Christmas 1957, said Jan.

00:45:58.792 --> 00:46:03.273
Yes, said Joseph.

00:46:03.333 --> 00:46:12.686
In October and November of that year, things got more and more dangerous for Lenke and me.

00:46:12.746 --> 00:46:18.837
Our friends told us, leave before the Russians get you.

00:46:18.897 --> 00:46:24.148
Get away to Austria and then to England.

00:46:24.208 --> 00:46:29.205
We didn't want to leave Czechoslovakia, of course.

00:46:29.265 --> 00:46:34.501
It was our home, but we couldn't stay.

00:46:34.561 --> 00:46:45.274
Our friends helped us, and Jan and I got across the border on the day before Christmas, December the 24th.

00:46:45.334 --> 00:46:47.444
It was night.

00:46:47.504 --> 00:46:55.246
There was no moon, and we got to Austria all right through the fields and the snow.

00:46:55.306 --> 00:47:02.554
But the next night, December the 25th, said Pavel.

00:47:02.614 --> 00:47:05.636
My grandmother told me the day.

00:47:05.696 --> 00:47:11.058
My mother died in a hospital bed in Prague, she said.

00:47:11.118 --> 00:47:15.270
Lenka died in the snow.

00:47:15.330 --> 00:47:20.541
On the road at the border, Josef said.

00:47:20.601 --> 00:47:32.884
She was so near Austria, so near us, with you, Pavel, on her back.

00:47:32.944 --> 00:47:48.874
The old man's voice stopped, and again, he put his head in his hands.

00:47:48.934 --> 00:48:02.504
Chapter 7 The music must come first.

00:48:02.564 --> 00:48:08.907
For some minutes, nobody in the rooms said anything.

00:48:08.967 --> 00:48:18.780
They looked at the old man in his chair, and they all thought about a snowy night in 1957.

00:48:18.840 --> 00:48:23.072
Then Parval turned to Jan.

00:48:23.132 --> 00:48:29.958
Let's forget 1957 for now, he said quietly.

00:48:30.018 --> 00:48:34.660
For me, this is a wonderful day.

00:48:34.721 --> 00:48:41.546
I have no family in Prague, My grandmother died many years ago.

00:48:41.606 --> 00:48:47.558
But now I have a brother, a father.

00:48:47.618 --> 00:48:52.269
He looked at Carol in her bed and smiled.

00:48:52.329 --> 00:49:00.382
And her sister, why did you come to the hospital to see me?

00:49:00.442 --> 00:49:02.372
Carol asked.

00:49:02.432 --> 00:49:05.932
You had an accident because of me.

00:49:05.992 --> 00:49:10.264
Pavel said, I knew that.

00:49:10.324 --> 00:49:21.204
You called to me and shouted, and then ran to me across the street, right in front of a bus.

00:49:21.264 --> 00:49:29.282
I didn't understand why, but I wanted to know that you were all right.

00:49:29.342 --> 00:49:33.225
Jan looked at Carol too.

00:49:33.285 --> 00:49:36.855
And are you all right, my love?

00:49:36.916 --> 00:49:38.146
I'm sorry.

00:49:38.166 --> 00:49:40.046
I forgot about you.

00:49:40.066 --> 00:49:46.398
I'm feeling very well, Carol said happily.

00:49:46.458 --> 00:49:53.529
Now I understand everything, so I feel much better.

00:49:53.589 --> 00:50:00.710
My husband is my husband again, and we have a new brother.

00:50:00.770 --> 00:50:05.012
Oh, but there is one thing.

00:50:05.072 --> 00:50:08.034
She looked at her new brother.

00:50:08.094 --> 00:50:16.048
Why is your name Parvel Brechter and not Parvel Vlach?

00:50:16.109 --> 00:50:20.350
The old man moved in his chair.

00:50:20.411 --> 00:50:29.123
Her name was Linker Brechter, he said quietly, before she married me.

00:50:29.184 --> 00:50:32.794
Yes, Pavel said.

00:50:32.854 --> 00:50:35.506
He looked at Carol.

00:50:35.567 --> 00:50:39.700
You see, my father didn't want me.

00:50:39.760 --> 00:50:41.272
I thought.

00:50:41.332 --> 00:50:44.904
So I didn't want my father's name.

00:50:44.964 --> 00:50:51.460
And when I was older, I changed it and took my mother's name.

00:50:51.520 --> 00:50:54.612
He turned to his father.

00:50:54.672 --> 00:50:58.264
I was an angry young man then.

00:50:58.324 --> 00:51:02.674
But now, no, said Joseph.

00:51:02.734 --> 00:51:04.634
Don't change it.

00:51:04.694 --> 00:51:07.195
It's a very good name.

00:51:07.255 --> 00:51:11.516
And you are Linka's son.

00:51:11.576 --> 00:51:17.938
Suddenly, the door opened and Mr. Rinaldi came in.

00:51:17.998 --> 00:51:24.290
Carol, he said, the doctor says that you are better.

00:51:24.350 --> 00:51:26.541
Is it true?

00:51:26.601 --> 00:51:29.333
You look wonderful.

00:51:29.394 --> 00:51:32.706
Can you play in the concert tonight?

00:51:32.766 --> 00:51:40.932
You see, I can't find another harpist and without a harp, the music.

00:51:40.992 --> 00:51:46.244
He saw everyone for the first time and stopped.

00:51:46.304 --> 00:51:51.108
Oh, I'm sorry, he said quickly.

00:51:51.168 --> 00:51:57.840
I see you have friends here, but you see, It's important.

00:51:57.900 --> 00:52:02.052
It's an important concert for my orchestra.

00:52:02.112 --> 00:52:05.522
And he stopped again.

00:52:05.582 --> 00:52:09.964
Why are you all laughing at me?

00:52:10.024 --> 00:52:13.915
Young stopped laughing first.

00:52:13.975 --> 00:52:23.564
Mr. Rinaldi, he said, you are the right man for Prague, the city of music.

00:52:23.624 --> 00:52:27.601
The music must come first.

00:52:27.662 --> 00:52:31.953
Carol, Mr. Analdi began.

00:52:32.013 --> 00:52:35.184
Carol turned to Jan.

00:52:35.245 --> 00:52:42.187
I feel very well now, and I'd like to play tonight.

00:52:42.247 --> 00:52:46.878
But I want all my family to come to the concert.

00:52:46.938 --> 00:52:54.212
My husband, my new brother, and their father.

00:52:54.272 --> 00:52:56.314
Can you all come?

00:52:56.374 --> 00:52:58.926
Please say yes.

00:52:58.986 --> 00:53:02.979
Jan looked at his father.

00:53:03.039 --> 00:53:06.222
Are you all right, Dad?

00:53:06.282 --> 00:53:09.563
Or are you feeling tired now?

00:53:09.624 --> 00:53:14.036
Shall we all go to Mr. Anaudie's concert?

00:53:14.096 --> 00:53:19.040
Three tickets, of course, for all Carol's family.

00:53:19.100 --> 00:53:22.051
Said Mr. Anaudie quickly.

00:53:22.111 --> 00:53:29.004
Christmas music in Prague again, Josef said slowly.

00:53:29.064 --> 00:53:37.610
And with my two sons, wonderful, wonderful.

00:53:37.670 --> 00:53:42.482
He smiled happily at Jan and Pavel.

00:53:42.542 --> 00:53:46.134
How can we say no?

00:53:46.194 --> 00:53:49.996
He asked.

00:53:50.056 --> 00:53:52.746
you

